<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="section-3" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Rational Expressions and Equations</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Another important type of algebraic expression is a rational expression. A rational expression is a ratio or fraction of polynomial expressions. One thing we have to be 
      careful about with rational expressions is that they have variables in the denominator and we cannot allow the denominator of the fraction to be zero.
    </p>
  </introduction>
